                <head>No. 74<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>Pursuant to the decision taken at the National Security Council meeting of
                    February 25, an <hi rendition="#italic">Ad Hoc</hi> Committee on NSC 143 was
                    established under the chairmanship of General Willis D. Crittenberger. The other
                    members of the committee were Charles B. Marshall, Department of State; Major
                    General Clark L. Ruffner, Department of Defense; Brigadier General John
                    Weckerling, Central Intelligence Agency; and Edmund Taylor, Psychological
                    Strategy Board. Colonel Roy A. Murray served as Executive Secretary. Records of
                    17 committee meetings between March 5 and April 17 are in S/S–NSC files, lot 63
                    D 351, NSC 143 Series. The records which appear on the following pages are the
                    minutes of the 7th, 10th, and 11th meetings. At the conclusion of the entire
                    series of meetings, the <hi rendition="#italic">Ad Hoc</hi> Committee drafted a
                    report of its findings. This report was accepted by the National Security
                    Council as the staff study on which was based the statement of policy in NSC
                    143/2, <ref target="#d80">Document 80</ref>.</p>
            </div>
